-- better-auth 1.7.7 (PR #244, ADR-0094). Generated by `drizzle-kit generate`; only this header is
-- hand-written. The snapshot is as generated.
--
-- better-auth 1.7.0–1.7.2 keyed a login account by (issuer, account_id) and wrote `issuer` on every
-- row (0000_init). 1.7.3 went back to 1.6's key, (provider_id, account_id), and writes `issuer` no
-- more: its check at start refuses a schema that still requires the column, and the NOT NULL would
-- fail every insert into account — every sign-up (an email one at /set-password, a social one at
-- its first sign-in) and every link.
-- - account_issuer_accountId_uidx and account.issuer go: the upgrade guide's clean-up, the column
--   with it (nothing reads it).
-- - account_providerId_accountId_uidx keeps the one row per login the dropped index kept:
--   better-auth refuses a lookup that finds two rows, so a second row from a race would shut the
--   member out. Each provider had one fixed issuer in 1.7.2 (credential → 'local:credential',
--   google → 'https://accounts.google.com', kakao and naver → 'local:oauth:<id>'), so every row the
--   old index took is unique on the new key too.
-- - Runs while the previous API (1.7.2) still serves: until deploy.sh replaces it, after `migrate`
--   and the seed, its adapter names the column in every account read and write, so its sign-ups,
--   sign-ins, links and password changes fail; sessions and GET /me do not (ADR-0046 D3's window,
--   as 0028's — ADR-0070 결과 3). An image from before 0047 cannot be redeployed over it.
DROP INDEX "account_issuer_accountId_uidx";--> statement-breakpoint
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "account_providerId_accountId_uidx" ON "account" USING btree ("provider_id","account_id");--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "account" DROP COLUMN "issuer";